MID_EV11_085_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_085_m01_001: Cai! Something's happening at Aurora's temple!
MID_EV11_085_m01_002: We don't know what's going on, but it seems like\nthe atmosphere there is getting tense.
MID_EV11_085_m01_030: We don't know what's going on, but it seems like\nthe atmosphere there is getting tense.
MID_EV11_085_m01_003: We better look into it. Let's go.
MID_EV11_085_m01_033: 
MID_EV11_085_m01_034: 
MID_EV11_085_m01_004: How many times must I inquire before I am granted\nan audience with Aurora?
MID_EV11_085_m01_005: Queen Theodora, it is as I have been telling you.
MID_EV11_085_m01_006: Aurora simply does not receive visitors.
MID_EV11_085_m01_007: Please, be aware of the many, er, witnesses here, and\nwithdraw peacefully.
MID_EV11_085_m01_008: I am a visiting head of state, entrusted by the Divine\nSovereign with oversight of the southern regions.
MID_EV11_085_m01_009: I demand either an audience or a clear explanation of\nthis obstinate refusal.
MID_EV11_085_m01_010: Is it Aurora's will that no one sees her, or yours?
MID_EV11_085_m01_011: Theodora's beyond upset. She's really angry!
MID_EV11_085_m01_032: Theodora's beyond upset. She's really angry!
MID_EV11_085_m01_012: If we don't put a stop to this now, it'll only get worse.
MID_EV11_085_m01_013: Bonaventure, what is Theodora so upset about?
MID_EV11_085_m01_014: Ah, young Cai. The short version of it is that we are\nin a precarious situation.
MID_EV11_085_m01_015: A delicate problem has arisen in the south. We must\nreturn to our kingdom with haste.
MID_EV11_085_m01_016: But Her Majesty will not leave before she can have\nan audience with Aurora, the daughter of Yu Phas.
MID_EV11_085_m01_017: The boss's arm has given her a real temper. If this\ngoes on, there could be, uh, casualties.
MID_EV11_085_m01_018: We really don't wanna go to war with the temples,\nbut that's where this is headed.
MID_EV11_085_m01_019: If that happened, I dunno if I'd have it in me to hold\nthe boss back anymore.
MID_EV11_085_m01_020: Hrm...
MID_EV11_085_m01_021: If you will not grant me entry, I shall force my\nway in. Are you prepared to stop me?
MID_EV11_085_m01_022: Um, excuse me, Theodora. Can I talk to you for a \nminute? In private?
MID_EV11_085_m01_023: You again. As you can see, I have pressing business\nhere. But very well, I shall hear you out.
MID_EV11_085_m01_024: Theodora, you just want to see Aurora, right?
MID_EV11_085_m01_025: Indeed. I must convey to Aurora how much she\nmeans to the people of Saramis.
MID_EV11_085_m01_026: I can get you in to see her. Follow me.
MID_EV11_085_m01_027: Ah! You? Are you quite sure about this?
MID_EV11_085_m01_028: I've no idea how you will accomplish this, but you\nhave earned my trust by now. Lead the way.
MID_EV11_056_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_056_m01_001: Thanks for trusting me, Theodora. We're here.
MID_EV11_056_m01_002: Oh, hello. I've never seen this girl before. Is she your\nwife, Cai?
MID_EV11_056_m01_042: Oh, hello. I've never seen this girl before. Is she your\nwife, Cai?
MID_EV11_056_m01_003: What? No!
MID_EV11_056_m01_004: Really? Well, you are at the age when relationships\nbecome important, after all.
MID_EV11_056_m01_043: Really? Well, you are at the age when relationships\nbecome important, after all.
MID_EV11_056_m01_005: Come on. I'm only 15.
MID_EV11_056_m01_006: "This girl"? I trust she wasn't referring to me.\nI must have misheard.
MID_EV11_056_m01_007: Cai, I hope there is a good explanation for you\nbringing me here.
MID_EV11_056_m01_008: Uh...I want to introduce you. Um, Queen Theodora,\nthe, er, Highness, from the kingdom of Saramis?
MID_EV11_056_m01_009: Oh, I see! You are very welcome. Thank you for\nmaking the effort to visit me.
MID_EV11_056_m01_044: Oh, I see! You are very welcome. Thank you for\nmaking the effort to visit me.
MID_EV11_056_m01_010: I've heard all about you, and not just from Cai.
MID_EV11_056_m01_045: I've heard all about you, and not just from Cai.
MID_EV11_056_m01_011: Theodora, this is the person you wanted to meet.\nMy mother...Aurora.
MID_EV11_056_m01_012: Excuse me?
MID_EV11_056_m01_013: It's a pleasure to meet you, Queen Theodora. And I\nassure you it's true. I am Cai's mother, Aurora.
MID_EV11_056_m01_014: What?! You are Aurora?! Then I have been\ninexcusably rude.
MID_EV11_056_m01_015: Don't worry about all that. Come to think of it, this\nreminds me of something you said a while back.
MID_EV11_056_m01_016: You wondered if my parents knew what I was up to.
MID_EV11_056_m01_017: How can you remember such trivial details?!\nI, ah, am sure your parents knew perfectly well.
MID_EV11_056_m01_018: Your Majesty is even more interesting than I\nhad imagined.
MID_EV11_056_m01_019: Please pardon my rudeness. I am still astonished to\nbe in your presence.
MID_EV11_056_m01_020: I have long wished that we would meet. My people\nare descended from the survivors of Damascar.
MID_EV11_056_m01_021: We owe everything to Yu Phas, and you are her\nsole daughter.
MID_EV11_056_m01_022: I have heard much of the bitter hardships you and\nyour people endured, Your Majesty.
MID_EV11_056_m01_023: It cheers me to know that you hold my mother so\ndeeply in your hearts after all this time.
MID_EV11_056_m01_024: Nnngh...
MID_EV11_056_m01_025: Your arm! Let me have a look.
MID_EV11_056_m01_026: You've been overdoing it, haven't you? We'll need to\ntake care of this immediately.
MID_EV11_056_m01_027: I've calmed the agitation in your right arm. This\nought to lighten your burden quite a bit.
MID_EV11_056_m01_028: The voice echoing in the depths of my soul,\ntempting me relentlessly, has been muffled.
MID_EV11_056_m01_029: You were prepared to die to meet the long-held\ndesire of your people, weren't you?
MID_EV11_056_m01_030: But you shouldn't be so reckless. You're still so young.
MID_EV11_056_m01_031: My mother wouldn't have wanted you to sacrifice\nyourself to see her properly worshipped. Nor would I.
MID_EV11_056_m01_033: Glad we got you fixed up, Theodora. You should be\ngood for a while now.
MID_EV11_056_m01_034: Cai...you have my utmost gratitude. Forgive me for\nall you have suffered on my behalf.
MID_EV11_056_m01_035: You don't seem like yourself when you bow your\nhead at me like that.
MID_EV11_056_m01_036: Reclining in your chair, leaning on an elbow with an\nI'm-in-charge attitude... That's the Theodora I know.
MID_EV11_056_m01_037: It's actually kind of comforting to me, imagining you\nbossing other people around.
MID_EV11_056_m01_038: Hehe. That is a generous sentiment from one\nso young.
MID_EV11_056_m01_039: Pardon me, Aurora, but I have urgent matters to\nattend to. I must take my leave.
MID_EV11_056_m01_040: Cai, should you ever find yourself in Saramis, I insist\nyou make an appearance at the palace.
MID_EV11_056_m01_041: You will be my special guest, and receive the\nwarmest welcome my people can provide.
MID_EV11_058_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_058_m01_001: Cai. I must ask, what will you do with yourself after\nthe games are finished?
MID_EV11_058_m01_002: I don't think we've talked about that yet.
MID_EV11_058_m01_003: If we win... When we win, we'll set you and Pop free.
MID_EV11_058_m01_004: I thought maybe the three of us could spend some\nquiet time together as a family.
MID_EV11_058_m01_005: We could do some traveling since, you know, you've\nbeen trapped here for so long now.
MID_EV11_058_m01_006: That would be so nice. You can't even imagine\nhow happy that would make me.
MID_EV11_058_m01_007: Oh...
MID_EV11_058_m01_008: Mom? Are you OK? Did I say something wrong?
MID_EV11_058_m01_009: Hehe. It's just, when you talk like that I'm reminded\nof conversations your father and I used to have.
MID_EV11_058_m01_010: Especially when we were making our plans to run\naway from Dagsion together.
MID_EV11_058_m01_011: He'd ask me about what I wanted to do with my\nfreedom. And we would talk about, well, everything.
MID_EV11_058_m01_012: But the way it played out, our pursuers were so\nrelentless, and we could never let our guard down.
MID_EV11_058_m01_013: We did have some fun days, though, even if my early\ncooking failures led to some...discomfort.
MID_EV11_058_m01_014: That sounds...nice, in a strange way. Even a\nstomachache can become a good memory, right?
MID_EV11_058_m01_015: Cai, do you think you can take me with you\nsometime...outside?
MID_EV11_058_m01_016: You bringing that girl to see me reminded me of\nold times.
MID_EV11_058_m01_017: I'd love to get out in the city, rub shoulders with\npeople, and maybe visit some markets.
MID_EV11_058_m01_018: I'll need to make a few preparations first, but let's try\nto have our day out sometime soon.
MID_EV11_059_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_059_m01_001: So this is what it's like underneath the arena now.
MID_EV11_059_m01_002: Gabriel, is it OK if I go see Pop today?
MID_EV11_059_m01_003: Back again? And you brought a lady? Y'know,\na dungeon's kind of a lousy place for a date, kid.
MID_EV11_059_m01_004: But you have the favor of the Lady of Lilies, so\nyou're free to go in.
MID_EV11_059_m01_005: As a matter of fact, she arrived a little while ago.\nMusta gone in to see the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV11_059_m01_006: Keep your nose clean, alright?
MID_EV11_059_m01_007: Of course. Thanks, Gabriel.
MID_EV11_059_m01_008: Every time he comes in here, he's got some new girl\nwith him. Strange kid.
MID_EV11_059_m01_009: Oh, hello. Interesting to see you here. I caught your\nlast match, you know.
MID_EV11_059_m01_010: Your battle against the queen of Saramis was truly\namazing. It sent shivers down my spine.
MID_EV11_059_m01_011: Hello, Iliana. Are you here to see Bertrand again?
MID_EV11_059_m01_012: Hehehe. The final match is next. Maybe you'll have\nto fight my White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV11_059_m01_013: No matter what, I'm sure it'll be an incredible fight\nremembered throughout the history of the arena.
MID_EV11_059_m01_014: Oh.
MID_EV11_059_m01_015: Have I had the pleasure of meeting you before?
MID_EV11_059_m01_016: No. Maybe. Probably not.
MID_EV11_059_m01_017: I see. Well, I'll bid you farewell. And I'll look forward\nto seeing you in action, young man.
MID_EV11_059_m01_018: Cai, do you know that woman?
MID_EV11_059_m01_019: Not well. Everyone calls her the Lady of Lilies.
MID_EV11_059_m01_020: She seems like someone important. She's the reason\nI can get into this place.
MID_EV11_059_m01_021: {SetColor=Gray}Lady of Lilies... I wonder what that means.{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_059_m01_022: {SetColor=Gray}And her face... Why does she look so much\nlike Mother?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV11_060_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_060_m01_001: Cai, don't you have better things to do than hang out\nin this place?
MID_EV11_060_m01_002: Listen. I'm not feeling too good today. How about\nyou come back another time?
MID_EV11_060_m01_003: You're acting like this because you don't want him to\nsee the bloodstains on your clothes, aren't you?
MID_EV11_060_m01_004: You haven't changed much. You still handle a\ndifficult situation in the clumsiest way possible. 
MID_EV11_060_m01_005: Aurora? What are you doing here?
MID_EV11_060_m01_006: Cai brought me along. Looks like you've lost even\nmore weight.
MID_EV11_060_m01_007: Well, happy birthday anyway, dear. I got this for you\nin town.
MID_EV11_060_m01_008: This... This is just like the one we got before.
MID_EV11_060_m01_009: Right. It looks like that one I bought you when we\nspent that day in the city so long ago.
MID_EV11_060_m01_010: I've been wanting to get you something to lift\nyour spirits.
MID_EV11_060_m01_011: I saw this, and it reminded me of that day.
MID_EV11_060_m01_012: As I recall, you got mad because the statue didn't\nlook like you. You said its cheeks were too puffy.
MID_EV11_060_m01_013: But I took a liking to it.
MID_EV11_060_m01_014: I gotta say, your timing is perfect. Your son broke the\nother one, that rascal.
MID_EV11_060_m01_015: Cai?! Is that true?
MID_EV11_060_m01_016: It was an accident. Pop never told me how special\nit was.
MID_EV11_060_m01_017: Thank you, Aurora. It's good to be reminded of\nbetter times.
MID_EV11_060_m01_018: You're still here? Look, something bad's going on\nup above!
MID_EV11_060_m01_019: This oughta work. C'mon, everybody, in here!
MID_EV11_060_m01_020: Where'd the old man go?
MID_EV11_060_m01_021: We don't need him. We're here for the treasure.
MID_EV11_060_m01_022: Where is it, boss?
MID_EV11_060_m01_023: There should be a big door in the level below this\none. We smash through it, and we'll get that treasure.
MID_EV11_060_m01_024: What in the world is happening?
MID_EV11_060_m01_025: It's unheard of. Bandits have taken over the arena.
MID_EV11_060_m01_026: We had a petty thief by the name of Gervasio locked\naway in here, but he busted out somehow.
MID_EV11_060_m01_027: Then he let his cronies in and took over the arena.\nThey blocked all the exits.
MID_EV11_060_m01_028: A bunch of folks are trapped inside. Guards, fighters,\neven the commissioner, Poloni.
MID_EV11_060_m01_029: I got the authority to release you, so...I am.\nTake care of these thugs!
MID_EV11_060_m01_030: Right. Our first order of business is probably\ncapturing the ringleader.
MID_EV11_060_m01_031: You clear this up, and Poloni's gonna owe you\nbig-time.
MID_EV11_060_m01_032: Count me in, Bertrand.
MID_EV11_060_m01_033: Castor and I are in too! This is so exciting!
MID_EV11_060_m01_034: Alright. If you're in, I'm in. Let's crack some heads.
MID_EV11_061_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_061_m01_001: What the hell's all this? Where's the treasure?
MID_EV11_061_m01_002: Hold on. What's this?
MID_EV11_061_m01_003: Is the whole thing made of orichalcum? Doesn't\nseem possible.
MID_EV11_061_m01_004: Is that the treasure? I've never heard of anything\nlike this.
MID_EV11_061_m01_005: You couldn't get that outta here with a hundred\nelephants. It's impressive though.
MID_EV11_061_m01_006: What are we gonna do, brother? The troops we got\nhere can't possibly carry it out.
MID_EV11_061_m01_007: We'll grab as much orichalcum as we can and escape\nthrough the tunnels before any do-gooders arrive.
MID_EV11_061_m01_008: Even a few armloads oughta keep us livin' the high\nlife for a decade.
MID_EV11_061_m01_009: I wouldn't be so sure. Hold it there.
MID_EV11_061_m01_010: Luck's run out, boys.
MID_EV11_061_m01_011: I had no idea this was under the arena.
MID_EV11_061_m01_023: Dead end! Heh heh heh. Now'd be the time to say\nyour prayers.
MID_EV11_061_m01_024: You're not gonna bother my big bro—not without\ngettin' your legs broke!
MID_EV11_061_m01_025: I'm stunned... This has been lying under the arena\nall along?
MID_EV11_061_m01_012: Th-that's the...the White-Maned Demon! They say he\nkilled a giant!
MID_EV11_061_m01_013: There were even rumors that he took out the\nlegendary Reaper.
MID_EV11_061_m01_014: Boss, this is no good. We gotta fold here. We can't\nwin this one.
MID_EV11_061_m01_015: Where's your backbone? Are we the Sour Milk Gang\nor aren't we?
MID_EV11_061_m01_016: Even the White-Maned Demon is human. And we've\ngot the numbers. We can't lose.
MID_EV11_061_m01_026: Heh heh HEH! Can't lose, he says! Maybe you don't\nknow what you're in for?
MID_EV11_061_m01_027: But yeah, alright. Let's put that to the test!
MID_EV11_061_m01_028: Look at this rabble. It's like we've wandered into a\ncasting call for moronic mob members.
MID_EV11_061_m01_029: As villains in The Rise of the White-Maned Demon,\nyou would be sorely deficient.
MID_EV11_061_m01_030: A shame too, as the backdrop is breathtaking!\nI'll have to make note of it for my next work...
MID_EV11_061_m01_017: They're terrified of you.
MID_EV11_061_m01_018: Hardly the first to react that way. If anything, your\nlack of concern is what's noteworthy.
MID_EV11_061_m01_019: Most want to steer clear of the White-Maned Demon.
MID_EV11_061_m01_020: Huh. You seem like a stand-up guy to me, but I know\nhow it goes...
MID_EV11_061_m01_021: You believe in yourself, do your best, but still end up\nmaking nothing but enemies. Pretty old story, really.
MID_EV11_061_m01_022: Pop, Bertrand. Enough with the chitchat.
MID_EV11_061_m01_031: You're workin' your jaws too much. Now we're gonna\nwipe out the whole lot of ya.
MID_EV11_062_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV11_062_m01_001: Dagda's cauldron... I hoped I'd never see this\nhorrific thing again.
MID_EV11_062_m01_002: It's a colossal execution device, built in Dagsion on\nthe orders of the Divine Emperor...my grandfather.
MID_EV11_062_m01_003: It devoured hundreds of thousands of people,\neventually including my mother, Yu Phas.
MID_EV11_062_m01_004: It's an abominable memory that will never fade,\nrooted in the very bowels of Dagsion.
MID_EV11_062_m01_005: Mom...
MID_EV11_062_m01_006: When Father ascended as the Divine Sovereign, his\nfirst act was sealing away this wicked thing.
MID_EV11_062_m01_007: Building the arena directly above it was an attempt\nto conceal its horror.
MID_EV11_062_m01_008: It was buried in hopes that only the city itself would\nremember it. There are few alive who know it exists.
MID_EV11_062_m01_009: Looks like the bigwigs have made their grand\nentrance at last.
MID_EV11_062_m01_010: All of you! Charge! Subdue the bandits!
MID_EV11_062_m01_011: Poloni, sir, the bandits have already been defeated.
MID_EV11_062_m01_012: Wh-what?
MID_EV11_062_m01_013: Right on time. We've subdued them. Find them some\nproper lodging, would you?
MID_EV11_062_m01_014: The White-Maned Demon... Wh-what are you doing\nout of your cell? Who has the keys?
MID_EV11_062_m01_015: I let him out. Figured we needed his help,\nconsidering the emergency.
MID_EV11_062_m01_016: You're not actually gonna complain about them\ntaking out the bandits, are you?
MID_EV11_062_m01_017: I assume we'll be receiving a monetary reward, yes?\nPer bandit defeated?
MID_EV11_062_m01_018: Oh... Uh... I'll have to speak with my boss about that.
MID_EV11_062_m01_019: Ha, that guy lost control the second things went bad.
MID_EV11_062_m01_020: The bandits ran right over him. I bet he was shaking\nin his boots.
MID_EV11_062_m01_021: Shush! Sometimes adults have to put up a brave\nfront to try and save face.
MID_EV11_062_m01_022: Don't make enemies of them. It's better to act like\nthey're doing us a favor.
MID_EV11_062_m01_023: Tialla really knows how to play grown-up games.
MID_EV11_062_m01_024: In any case, you all need to get back in your cells.
MID_EV11_062_m01_025: And what are children doing here? This is no place\nfor them.
MID_EV11_062_m01_026: We were helping Gabriel and got caught up in\nthe trouble.
MID_EV11_062_m01_027: We were so scared, sir. We just want to go home.
MID_EV11_062_m01_028: Yes, yes, I understand. Off you go then, children.
MID_EV11_062_m01_029: Yes, sir. Thank you, sir.
MID_EV11_062_m01_030: Castor, please just hold on a little longer. Cai and I\nwill do everything we can to save you.
MID_EV11_062_m01_031: Never thought you'd be the one saving me. Gotta say\nI'm a little impressed.
MID_EV11_062_m01_032: Cai, thank you. I'm so glad we got to go out today.
MID_EV11_062_m01_033: But I'd better get back before Centurio realizes that I\nsnuck out.
MID_EV11_062_m01_034: I had fun with you today, Mom. Can't wait to save\nPop together.